ilable). Privacy Policy Thank you - we'll be in touch soon. This is Wichita State University Stuff about WSU with links WSU Fast Facts Home (wichita.edu) Higher Learning Commission (HLC) (wichita.edu) Stuff about WSU with links Vision, mission and values (wichita.edu) Office of the President, Dr. Richard Muma (wichita.edu) WSU Strategic Plan (wichita.edu) WSU Public Records (wichita.edu) Stuff about WSU with links Talent Frequently Asked Questions (wichita.edu) Know Your Rights: Workplace Discrimination is Illegal (eeoc.gov) Background Checks (wichita.edu) Benefits WSU Employee Benefits Guide ICAA Employee Benefits Guide WSU Employee Benefits Webpage Tuition Assistance Program Leave Administration WSU Core Vision, mission & values Office of the President WSU Strategic Plan WSU Public Records Hiring Preference Info Hiring Preferences Wichita State University Home Page Wichita – Where Opportunity is Growing Stuff about Wichita with links Choose Wichita Stuff about Wichita with links Wichita, KS | Official Website Stuff about Wichita with links City of Wichita - Splash (myvscloud.com) Wichita - Where Opportunity is Growing Choose Wichita Wichita, KS | Official Website Wichita City - Splash Recent Job Openings Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks.\n\nAll majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Custodial Lead Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Wichita – Where Opportunity is Growing Choose Wichita Wichita, KS | Official Website City of Wichita - Splash Cost of Living Have Questions? Check our frequently asked questions ( FAQs ). Wichita State Human Resources Website If at any time you have questions or issues with completing tasks, please reach out to Human Resources for assistance: WSU Human Resources: (316) 978-3065 or email employment@wichita.edu (Athletics staff should reach out to WSU HR) WSU Industry and Defense Programs Human Resources: (316) 978-5386 or email careers@idp.wichita.edu . Notice of Nondiscrimination: Wichita State University Notice of Nondiscrimination Statement EEO Statement: Wichita State University is an equal employment and affirmative action employer. Qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment regardless of age (40 years or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, gender, gender expression, gender identity, genetic information, marital status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, or status as a veteran. Persons with disabilities requesting accommodations in the application or interview process, please notify Human Resources at (316) 978-3065 or email employment@wichita.edu . Concerns related to discrimination may be directed to the Office of Civil Rights, Title IX & ADA Compliance (CTAC) . Supplemental Information Wichita State University Employment Compliance Resources Wichita State University participates in E-Verify , which is an internet-based system that compares information from an employee's Form I-9, Employment Eligibility Verification, to data from U.S. Department of Homeland Security and Social Security Administration records to confirm employment eligibility. LCA/PERM Notices At this time, the University has placed the process for sponsoring H-1B sponsorships on hold so that we may assess the feasibility of, and processes for, such sponsorships. We are working to establish updated processes and guidelines and will update this site when we have further information to share. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Not sure if Wichita is right for you?  Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 627e1b67 Last Name (required) 6e7bb262 Email (required) efbbaa43 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. 