    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/custodian-specialist-senior-wichita-kansas-united-states-2c899695-3e1b-4a82-8b33-729815da164e": {
      "title": "Custodian Specialist, Senior",
      "description": "Custodian Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Custodian Specialist, Senior Physical Plant | Staff Custodian Specialist, Senior 499389 Staff Add to favorites View favorites Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $16.49 plus $.60 per hour shift differential and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 3:00 pm - 11:30 pm Monday - Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story When campus floors need expert care and cleaning equipment needs a skilled hand, our Custodian Specialist, Senior steps in to make it happen. You’re the kind of person who takes pride in a gleaming hallway, a freshly waxed floor, and a vacuum that hums like new. You know your way around scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors, and when something breaks, you don’t just report it, you help fix it. You research parts and coordinate repairs to keep our custodial equipment running like a dream. When disaster strikes, like a spill, a flood, or a mess that needs immediate attention, you’re the calm in the chaos, restoring order with precision and care. You handle specialty cleaning chemicals with confidence, maintain upholstery and furnishings, and ensure every space you touch is safe, clean, and welcoming. Because for you, it’s not just about cleaning, it’s about creating spaces people feel good walking into. This position also comes with a robust benefits package (effective on your first day) and generous paid time off. Job Summary Performs specialized custodial services, such as maintenance and repair of custodial equipment, floor cleaning and finishing equipment, carpet and upholstery maintenance equipment. Essential Functions Maintains and performs minor repairs on custodial equipment, such as vacuums, floor and carpet cleaners, etc. Completes basic maintenance on floor care equipment. Researches sources and specifications to order parts for equipment repair and maintenance. Performs specialized custodial services such as floor cleaning and finishing, carpet and upholstery maintenance, cleaning building furnishings and/or procedures using specialty cleaning chemicals. Utilizes cleaning machinery such as scrubbers, buffers, and carpet extractors for floor care maintenance. Provides all floor care services including strip, wax, carpet cleaning and may provide disaster recovery for affected flooring. Cleans and services assigned areas in University buildings and maintains sufficient stock and supplies for the proper performance of these duties. Shovels and removes snow and ice from designated areas such as roofs, sidewalks and entryways as required. Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Two (2) years of experience in custodial equipment repair Required License/Certifications/Training: Valid Driver's License Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of operation and care of equipment, including, but not limited to: vacuum cleaners, scrubbing machines, polishing machines, and other janitorial equipment. Ability to work effectively with fellow workers and others. Ability to lift and carry heavy objects. Ability to understand and follow explicit instructions, both in oral and written form. Ability and willingness to perform any of a variety of routine cleaning tasks. Additional Information: Due to ITAR regulations, the chosen candidate must be a US Citizen to be considered for this role. Physical Requirements: Ability to position self for inspection, construction or maintenance of equipment and/or buildings including confined, elevated and loud noise spaces. Frequent 60-90% Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Rare 0-30% Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Rare 0-30% Ability to drive state vehicle. Rare 0-30% Ability to remove snow and ice from designated areas. Rare 0-30% Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Rare 0-30% Additional Physical Requirement: Heavy Work: Exerting up to 100 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 50 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 20 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) c57535c0 Last Name (required) 2b787c84 Email (required) 16bf3f01 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 7f0fce69 Last Name (required) 737fe181 Email (required) eece585e Job Alert b24d11db Finalize your job alert by