    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/environmental-health-and-safety-compliance-specialist-senior-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior",
      "description": "Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior Physical Plant | Staff Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist, Senior 499394 Staff Add to favorites View favorites Department: Facilities Services Campus Location: Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type: Full Time Pay: Starting at $29.45 per hour and commensurate with experience Work Schedule: 7:45 am - 4:30 pm Monday - Friday; work is performed on-site and in person. Export Compliance Requirement: This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story We are excited to announce an opportunity for a Senior Environmental Health and Safety Compliance Specialist to join our university community and play a vital role in fostering a safe, healthy, and compliant campus environment. This position coordinates with various areas to complete assigned environmental health and safety functions and inspections. Provides guidance and assistance and is responsible for promoting a safe and healthy workplace. Implements plans based on contracts, regulations, applicable laws and audit/inspection results to ensure that compliance is maintained. May provide training to employees in areas including, but not limited to, environmental, health and safety management best practices, and assisting with hazard identification and control. Job Summary Coordinates with various areas to complete assigned environmental health and safety functions and inspections. Provides guidance and assistance and is responsible for promoting a safe and healthy workplace. Implements plans based on contracts, regulations, applicable laws and audit/inspection results to ensure that compliance is maintained. May provide training to employees in areas including, but not limited to, environmental, health and safety management best practices, and assisting with hazard identification and control. Essential Functions • Leads and/or coordinates investigations of safety related incidents involving applicable University and/or community partners. Audits and ensures safety plans are in compliance with applicable laws and regulations. • Conducts audits of lab/department. Generates audit reports for corrective action as needed. • Maintains records for and ensures compliance with regulatory requirements. Communicates on safety related needs and develops program action plans. • Reviews and analyzes safety-related data. Prepares reports for regulatory agencies, committees and/or leadership. • Manages a hazardous materials and waste program that complies with all regulatory and requirements. • Provides educational training related to safety and emergency preparedness practices. • Coordinates and/or facilitates project tasks as assigned; Documents and tracks project progress compared to goal Required Education and Experience: High school diploma or equivalent Seven (7) years of related experience. Every 30 hours of college coursework can be substituted for one (1) year of experience, up to 120 hours. Knowledge, Skills and Abilities: Knowledge of deep, practical understanding of local, state, and federal regulations (e.g., OSHA, EPA, DOT). Knowledge of occupational health hazards, including chemical exposure limits, ergonomics, and noise/air monitoring. Ability to perform Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and develop corrective and preventive actions. Knowledge and proficiency in utilizing EHS software platforms, analyzing safety metrics, and generating compliance reports. Ability to coach, influence, and drive a proactive safety culture across all levels of the organization—from floor workers to senior executives. Skill to translate complex technical and regulatory findings into actionable, clear policies and training programs. Preferred Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in science related field. Additional Information: Due to ITAR regulations, the chosen candidate must be a US Citizen to be considered for this role. Physical Requirements: Ability to ascend and descend ladders and/or stairs. Frequent 60-90% Ability to inspect work, materials, equipment, and/or supplies and identify any errors, needs, and/or determining factors. Frequent 60-90% Ability to remain in a stationary position. Rare 0-30% Ability to use tools, equipment, and technology necessary to do the job. This includes dexterity in instrument manipulation. Frequent 60-90% Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Frequent 60-90% Additional Physical Requirement: Medium Work: Exerting up to 50 pounds of force occasionally and/or up to 20 pounds of force frequently, and/or up to 10 pounds of force to constantly move objects. Apply Now First Name (required) bead56e2 Last Name (required) ec32c31a Email (required) f44cb236 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) d4c8dcdd Last Name (required) 5c98ecaf Email (required) 872c3498 Job Alert 6980be6b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Staff Staff Department(s) Physical Plant Physical Plant Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) 1c1d4f42 Last Name (required) 5fcfd416 Email (required) 3a152b99 Send This Job To: e9f7eb39 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks.\n\nAll majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Custodial Lead Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Not sure if Wichita is right for you?  Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 765d184b Last Name (required) c1702c2c Email (required) 842555c5 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept Please choose a department(s)"
