    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-darc-design-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR DARC Design Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR DARC Design Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR DARC Design Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR DARC Design Student Assistant 496792 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department Engineering Design and Mod Team Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $14 - 22 per hour Work Schedule 20 - 25 hours per week based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The Engineering Design and Mod team is looking for a student assistant to help with daily tasks. Job Duties This position will support various diverse program efforts as a design assistant. Tasks include detail modeling of airframe structural/system details, drawing creation using dimensioning and tolerancing, and modelling parts from existing scans and drawings. Extensive design handbooks and recommended practices are used to efficiently design metallic parts, composite parts, and system components. The design assistant will execute changes to CATIA and 3DX models, drawings and other documents in support of the product and engineering team. Additional Requirements The design student assistant designs structure, mechanical, systems, and interior components on various company projects and programs across the entire life cycle of design and development. Design activity includes primary structure, systems, interiors, and standard parts libraries. The intern will work within a team environment and be expected to perform independent research activity, communicate with team effectively, and work to specified schedules and timelines. • Working toward a degree in mechanical or aerospace engineering. Sophomore or higher preferred. • Experience and interest in 3D CAD tools (3DExperience, CATIA V5, Siemens NX, Solidworks, etc.) • Experience and interest in mechanical systems and/or structure design/build. • Experience with Microsoft Office (word, excel, PowerPoint). • Excellent writing and communication skills. • Excellent time management, critical thinking and problem-solving skills. • Self-motivated and driven to produce high quality work on schedule. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information Apply Now First Name (required) af292049 Last Name (required) 4baeccb6 Email (required) 8bbec0a2 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 6914943b Last Name (required) 1dcb1a8d Email (required) ea996609 Job Alert fda3effe Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Student Student Department(s) NIAR Institute NIAR Institute Send Please wait... Done 