    "https://jobs.wichita.edu/jobs/niar-apex-engineering-student-assistant-wichita-kansas-united-states": {
      "title": "NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR APEX Engineering Student Assistant 499043 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department NIAR APEX Advanced Prod Execution Campus Location Wichita, KS - WSU Main Campus Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 20 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story NIAR’s APEX lab is looking for students to work with multiple lab capabilities for various projects at HAMR. Students may be required to learn about CAD and other software products and hardware. They will support a variety of projects and programs for the lab. Their task may range from classroom support and project research to direct industry program support. Employees will be expected to assist lab staff in any way possible to help make the lab successful, presentable to customers, and accomplish projects in a timely manner. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties · Support staff with reverse engineering projects. · Interpret existing engineering and quality data. · Model components from various data sources. · Assist staff with research project development. · Assisting staff on the industry level support. · Operate and help maintain tools and equipment. · Help keep a clean and safe work environment. · Assisting staff with the development of training materials. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications · Experience utilizing a CAD software program. · Excellent oral and written communication skills. · Proficiency with Microsoft Office Products. · Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings and bill of material systems. · Have great attention to detail. · Ability to lift and carry up to 25lbs. · Ability to work with complex systems. · Able to work 20+ hours each week. · Effectively prioritize and manage workflow. · Ability to work independently on extensive tasks. Additional Information Students must have their own transportation, as some local travel between facilities may be required. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks.\n\nAll majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Custodial Lead Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and 