      "title": "NIAR ETL Student Engineering Assistant",
      "description": "NIAR ETL Student Engineering Assistant - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode NIAR ETL Student Engineering Assistant NIAR Institute | Student NIAR ETL Student Engineering Assistant 497161 Student Add to favorites View favorites Department NIAR Environmental Test Lab Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $13 - $18 per hour Work Schedule Based on class schedule Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story The NIAR ETL is looking for a student assistant to help with testing aircraft components. Job Summary A student assistant will carry out administrative and technical tasks requested by a supervisor. Depending on the area the student assistant is employed in, they may assist and mentor other students or provide support throughout the campus in various forms. Job Duties Assist test engineers with industry standards aircraft component certification testing, Operate, maintain, and repair test equipment, prepare test setups, and test fixturing, maintain lab organization. Required Education High school diploma or equivalent Additional Requirements Must be a motivated, detail-oriented, and hands-on person willing to continuously learn and improve their skills. Preferred Qualifications CAD experience Machining and/or experience with tools and soldering Knowledge of standard test equipment (multimeters, oscilloscopes, signal generators/analyzers, data acquisition systems) Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment, including but not limited to phones, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks.\n\nAll majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Custodial Lead Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"
