ces. Additional Requirements Associate's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field (minimum 60 credit hours completed). 6 months experience working with students in grades 6-12. Valid Driver's license required. Must be able to escort students on campus visits - which may include lots of walking. May be asked to make community and school presentations. Overnight travel to training and conferences may be required. Required Experience This is specific to each position and department. See additional requirements and/or preferences. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Education, Counseling, Social Services or related field Additional Information 10 hours per week (20 per pay period). Candidate will set office hours with supervisor. Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position. Ability to operate a computer and other office equipment including but not limited to phone, printers, copiers, and calculators. Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) f6ca1777 Last Name (required) 9ee4340d Email (required) 7e8dcad6 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 812d6209 Last Name (required) 02b206ee Email (required) e72c7777 Job Alert dde00570 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Strategic Engagement & Planning Strategic Engagement & Planning 