      "description": "JAKS Construction Coordinator - Wichita, Kansas, United States social--blog Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Quick Links Close Menu Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal Why Wichita State University View\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tAll Jobs My Profile Leadership Innovation at WSU Research Directories Give to WSU myWSU OneStop Academic Calendar Apply Now! A-Z Directory Blackboard Calendar of Events Office Hours Policies and Procedures Schedule of Courses Shocker Store Student Webmail Technology HelpDesk Transfer to WSU University Libraries Close Menu Careers Faculty Staff Internal View All Jobs My Profile Kiosk mode JAKS Construction Coordinator Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm | Temporary JAKS Construction Coordinator 499286 Temporary Add to favorites View favorites Department Ennovar Campus Location Wichita, KS - Other Wichita Location Hire Type Part Time Pay $15 - 18 per hour Work Schedule Flexible Export Compliance Requirement This position requires access to EAR or ITAR controlled technologies. Applicants are required to be eligible for employment under U.S. export control laws and must meet the requirement of being a “U.S. Citizen”. Job Story Ennovar is looking for a Coordinator to work at JAKS Construction. Job Duties * Assist with creating and maintaining project schedules, task lists, and documentation in JobTread. * Coordinate with subcontractors and suppliers regarding project timelines, deliveries, quotes, and required documents. * Participate in site visits and inspections and help maintain daily logs, project photos, and progress updates. * Support the completion of punch lists, closeout documents, and client communications. * Assist with quantity takeoffs using project plans and specifications. * Request, collect, and organize subcontractor and supplier pricing. * Help prepare project estimates and maintain current material pricing information. * Assist with developing scopes of work, proposals, and presentation materials. * Support lead intake, follow-up, and organization of the sales pipeline. * Attend networking and community events with team members. * Help collect client reviews, referrals, and testimonials. Preferred Qualifications * Currently pursuing or recently completed a degree in Construction Management, Engineering, Business, or a related field; equivalent hands-on experience or interest in the trades may be considered. * Strong organizational skills, attention to detail, and ability to follow through on assigned tasks. * Ability and willingness to learn new software, including JobTread, spreadsheets, and email platforms. * Strong written and verbal communication skills. * Reliable, self-motivated, coach-able, and able to work both independently and collaboratively. * Valid driver’s license and reliable transportation required for travel to customer and project sites. * Ability to work on active job sites, including walking, standing, occasional lifting, and exposure to varying weather conditions. Additional Information Work is performed on site at JAKS Construction 5025 E Kellogg Dr. Wichita, KS. Physical Requirements Ability to communicate with others and accurately exchange information. Apply Now First Name (required) a5164d95 Last Name (required) 2a50a7b1 Email (required) a1ad3c84 Apply Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Sign Up for Job Alerts! First Name (required) 3f5cf3ad Last Name (required) 1a86d4f5 Email (required) 6c90c36e Job Alert 04a20854 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Temporary Temporary Department(s) Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Share This Job With Someone Else! First Name (required) af5e1afc Last Name (required) b11904ce Email (required) a9e4eaaa Send This Job To: 2351a577 Share Now! Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy We've sent this job to the email provided! Not the right fit? Search all jobs here. Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Recommended Jobs Work Study Only- Student Assistant- Business Student Success Center Looking for a flexible, on campus job to help develop your professional and customer service skills while working in a friendly and supportive environment? The Barton School of Business Student Success Center in Woolsey Hall is looking for a work study eligible student assistant to join our team to help staff our front desk to welcome guests, schedule student appointments, and assist with outreach to current and prospective students among other tasks.\n\nAll majors are invited to apply! Normal office hours are Monday through Friday from 8 AM to 5 PM but work schedules are flexible around your class schedule. Student workers can expect to be scheduled 10-20 hours per week on average. Must be federal work study eligible. IDP Project Coordinator - Advanced Materials Research Join the innovative team at NIAR’s Advanced Materials Research group and help drive cutting‑edge projects that shape the future of aerospace and advanced manufacturing. We’re looking for a proactive Project Manager who thrives in a collaborative, fast‑paced environment and enjoys turning complex ideas into successful, well‑executed outcomes. If you’re motivated by meaningful work, enjoy partnering with experts across disciplines, and want to be part of a mission-focused research organization, we’d love to hear from you. Custodial Lead Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Lead, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment. And the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. Custodial Supervisor, Second Shift Join a team that takes pride in maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment for students, faculty, and staff.\n\nAs a Custodial Supervisor, you will play a vital role in the upkeep of our university facilities by performing specialized custodial services and ensuring the proper operation and maintenance of custodial equipment.\n\nAnd the best part? You’ll enjoy a robust benefits package effective on your first day, supporting your health, well-being, and future, because we believe in taking care of the people who take care of our campus. 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Not sure if Wichita is right for you?  Sign up to receive emails from our Talent team to learn more about what it's like working here. First Name (required) 4afc1764 Last Name (required) dab8e547 Email (required) 1544a4b6 Send Please wait... Done Not You? By submitting this form and including your phone number, you consent to receive text messages related to available jobs and information about working at Wichita State University.  Message & data rates may apply.  Message frequency varies.  Unsubscribe at any time by replying STOP or clicking the unsubscribe link (where available). Privacy Policy Thank you Close Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do 