23 items) 23 Strategic Enrollment (1 items) 1 Strategic Enrollment Mgmt (6 items) 6 Student Affairs (College) (6 items) 6 Women's Sports/Activities (2 items) 2 WSU Police Department (3 items) 3 Search by job title, location, department, category, etc. Search Sort by: Last Updated Last Updated: Newest to Oldest Last Updated: Oldest to Newest Title: A-Z Title: Z-A FirePoint Program Student Assistant 499406 Wichita Student FirePoint Innovations FirePoint Innovations is looking for a Program Student Assistant. Read more Administrative Specialist 499204 Wichita Athletics Staff Temporary Administrative and Support Wichita State Intercollegiate Athletic Association, Inc, is searching for a talented administrative specialist. We deliver memorable experiences that connect all to Shocker Nation Through a Shared Sense of Pride & Passion. Read more Student Assistant Lifeguard 499393 Wichita Student Student Affairs (College) Lifeguards are responsible for ensuring patron safety by monitoring aquatic areas, enforcing facility rules, and preventing accidents. Primary duties include scanning water for distressed swimmers, performing rescues, administering CPR/first aid, and maintaining safety equipment, alongside assisting with water chemistry checks and cleaning. Read more NBE Student Assistant WSU 0350R 499383 Wichita Student College of Liberal Arts & Sciences The Anthropology Student Assistant provides administrative, academic, and operational support to faculty, staff, and students within the Department of Anthropology. This position offers students an opportunity to gain professional experience in higher education while contributing to the daily functions of the department. Duties may include research or clerical duties to include data collection, management, laboratory or office operations, event assistance, data entry, and support for departmental projects and activities. Students assistants will be directly supervised by a faculty member in the Department of Anthropology. Read more NBE Lecturer WSU 0237L 499382 Wichita Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer College of Fine Arts Lecturers in the School of Digital Arts are expected to teach media arts courses as assigned following the prescribed curriculum as set forth in the course syllabus. The lecturer’s responsibilities include developing course materials, inspiring meaningful discussions, grading assignments, and providing feedback on student work. Lecturers are also expected to complete any requisite training as assigned by Wichita State University and the College of Fine Arts. If for some reason a lecturer is unable to make a class meeting, they must work with the program coordinator of their area to find appropriate coverage of materials. Read more Senior Contracts and Grants Specialist 499112 Wichita Staff Office of Research (College) In this senior-level role, you will provide comprehensive pre-award support for primarily grant and contract applications submitted on behalf of Wichita State University. Are you a problem solver? Enjoy the challenge of multiple projects and meeting their deadlines? This position will be responsible for the development, implementation and oversight of pre-award grant and contract functions, including ensuring all applications comply with sponsor and University guidelines, and State and Federal rules and regulations. In this role, you will be part of a team that makes it possible for Wichita State and our industry partners to conduct research and projects that will improve and change the community of Wichita, health, education, and technology for Kansas, the US and possibly the world! Read more IDP Export Control Manager 499363 Wichita Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration Join a dynamic research environment where innovation meets compliance. The Export Control Manager serves as a trusted expert and key partner across the university, ensuring groundbreaking research and global collaborations align with federal export control regulations. In this role, you’ll shape and lead the university’s export control program, advise faculty and researchers on complex regulatory requirements, manage critical licensing processes, and maintain the university’s ITAR registration. If you’re energized by problem‑solving, collaboration, and supporting research that pushes boundaries, this position offers a meaningful opportunity to make an impact. Read more NIAR Aerospace Painter - Composites 499057 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The Aerospace Painter and Laboratory Technician supports NIAR Composites by preparing surfaces, mixing and applying aerospace coatings, and conducting performance and flammability testing in accordance with industry and FAA standards. The role also assists with laboratory operations, equipment maintenance, hazardous waste handling, and training of students on safe and proper procedures. Read more Program Counselor, College Readiness/Retention Programs 498700 Wichita Staff Strategic Engagement & Planning Be the Reason a Student Says, “I’m Going to College.”\n\nIf you’re the kind of person who sees potential before others do…\nIf you believe access to education shouldn’t depend on zip code…\nIf you’re energized by mentoring youth and watching confidence grow in real time…\n\nTRIO Talent Search is looking for you!\n\nAssigned Schools:\nMarshall Middle School and North High School (plus walk-in support as needed)\n\nThis isn’t a desk job. It’s boots-on-the-ground, sleeves-rolled-up, future-building work. You’ll work directly with middle and high school students, many of whom will be first-generation college students, guiding them toward academic persistence, high school graduation, and postsecondary enrollment. You’ll serve approximately 290 students annually, ensuring each one receives meaningful, documented, and compliant federal TRIO services. The heart of this job? Relationships.\n\nWhat You’ll Actually Be Doing:\nCollaborate with school administrators and community partners\nIdentify eligible students for the program & monitor their academic progress (intervening when needed)\nBuilding partnerships & relationships along the way at various levels\nMaintaining accurate student records and ensuring federal compliance\nYes, there’s documentation — because impact matters, and so does accountability.\n\nYou'll Thrive Here If You:\nConnect easily with youth across diverse backgrounds\nKnow how to balance encouragement with structure\nCan pivot quickly when student needs shift (because they will)\nAre organized enough to manage data while staying fully present with students\nUnderstand referral networks and aren’t afraid to collaborate\nBelieve that mentorship can literally change a life trajectory\nYou are intentional. Strategic. Consistent.\n\nIn a world where conversations about equity, opportunity gaps, and educational access dominate headlines, this is where the real work happens, one student at a time. If you’re ready to build futures, we want to hear from you.\nApply. Mentor. Advocate. Change trajectories! Read more Veterans Academic Advisor- Veterans Upward Bound 499054 Wichita Academic/Student Support Adjunct Faculty/Lecturer Management/Administration Office/Administrative Support Staff Show More Show Less Strategic Engagement & Planning Your Mission\n\nYou’ll work exclusively with military-affiliated students, providing wraparound services, start-to-finish support, from certification of benefits to graduation and beyond. When veteran and military-affiliated students transition into college life, they often face unique challenges related to academic planning, benefit navigation, and adjustment to civilian and campus culture. This role provides individualized academic guidance and support to help these students succeed. This is not a transactional advising role. You’ll serve as a constant throughout a student’s academic journey; someone they can trust to help them navigate both higher education systems and other military benefit programs with clarity and care. Read more College Access Advisor - Salina 498733 Wichita Staff Strategic Engagement & Planning Give me a S, give me an A, give me a L, give me an I, give me a N, give me an A! SALINA peeps, are you able to connect with students, be their cheerleader. Can you take students hand to guide them through the processes to help them meet their college dream goals? Do you believe every student deserves access to opportunities that extend beyond their current circumstances? You will need energy, passion and enthusiasm in this journey, come join this exciting adventure in helping make dreams come true. WE NEED YOU!\nKansas Kids @ GEAR UP is seeking a passionate, relationship-driven College Access Advisor to serve students in foster care throughout the Salina region. This role is an opportunity where you can make a direct impact by helping students navigate the education system while building consistent, meaningful connections that support their path after high school. You will need to be able to transport students safely and efficiently to and from events.\nOur program serves students in grades 7 through their first year of college, equipping them with the academic support, life skills, and guidance needed to graduate and pursue postsecondary education.\n\nSalina needs to be your town and community for this story to be successful! Read more NIAR 3-Axis CNC Machinist 499196 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is a fast-growing area within WSU, known globally for our expertise in the most critical areas of aerospace research and development. The Advanced Machining and Prototyping Lab is looking for CNC Machinist with 3-Axis experience to join our team. This position is located at our Park City, KS location. Read more Emergency Communications Specialist 499325 Wichita Staff WSU Police Department Why Choose Wichita State University Police Department?\nAs an Emergency Dispatcher, you'll be at the center of public safety operations, handling emergency and non-emergency calls, dispatching police officers and other resources, monitoring communications systems, and providing critical support during emergencies.\nThis position is ideal for individuals who:\n- Communicate clearly and professionally\n- Thrive in fast-paced environments\n- Possess strong problem-solving skills\n- Remain calm during stressful situations\n- Have a passion for public service and helping others Read more Talent Consultant- HR Specialist 499326 Wichita Staff Culture and HR Wichita State continues to innovate, evolve and shift!\nWorking for us follows along those lines, to ensure employees are able to do what is needed of them in their role.\n\nThe Talent team provides \"one-stop\" service and support for the university's hiring needs. Whether this be for students, returning employees, once a year hires, or all together new to us. Read more GTA- Indirect School of Art, Design and Creative Industries (Fall 2026) 499135 Wichita Student College of Fine Arts School of Art, Design and Creative Industries Indirect Teaching Assistantship (GTA-Indirect) Read more Graduate Teaching Assistant - Indirect 499307 Wichita Student College of Liberal Arts & Sciences A Graduate Teaching Assistant (GTA) focused on indirect teaching supports academic courses behind the scenes without leading front-of-class lectures, centering on grading, course material preparation, and Blackboard administration. The primary function of a graduate teaching assistant (GTA) is to assist with instruction. GTAs have the latitude to make independent decisions, use judgment and exercise discretion when dealing with student matters. The main purpose and responsibility of GTAs is to impart knowledge or training to students at Wichita State University Read more Peer Tutor - TRIO Student Support Services 499290 Wichita Student Strategic Engagement & Planning Are you passionate about helping others succeed? As a tutor with TRIO Student Support Services, you'll play an important role in supporting fellow WSU students as they work toward their academic goals. You'll get the opportunity to empower first-generation, limited-income, and students of disability status to feel confident in their studies. This is more than a job — it’s a chance to be a mentor, advocate, and champion for student success. Along the way, you'll strengthen your own communication and leadership skills in an experience that will benefit you long after graduation.\n\nIf you're reliable, organized, patient, and a great communicator, we want you on our team -- Apply today! Read more NBE Student Assistant - Work Study 0350W 499271 Wichita Student College of Fine Arts Work Study Eligible students needed in the School of Art, Design and Creative Industries office for office coverage and customer service.\n\nOffice Assistant Students must be available for morning hours. Must have knowledge of Microsoft Excel and Adobe Creative Cloud. Graphic Design experience a plus. Read more IDP Power BI Data Analyst 499320 Wichita Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration The Power BI Data Analyst supports a rapidly growing operation within the aerospace industry by transforming complex financial, operational, and program level data into clear, actionable insights. This role develops and maintains enterprise dashboards, data models, and analytics solutions that enhance financial transparency, strengthen decision-making, and drive optimized performance across diverse aerospace programs and business units. Read more Sports Facility Operations Manager 499109 Wichita Staff Student Affairs (College) The Facility Operations Coordinator provides comprehensive leadership and oversight for all Campus Recreation facilities, including the 166,000 sq. ft. Heskett Center, three Metroplex Playfields, and all on-campus pickleball and tennis facilities. This position ensures safe, efficient, and customer-focused daily operations while managing key departmental functions such as facility rentals, F45 programming, accounts receivable, and wellness services. The role supports a high-quality recreation environment through operational excellence and alignment with university policies. Read more NIAR Teardown Mechanic 499333 Wichita Aviation Staff NIAR Institute The National Institute for Aviation Research (NIAR) is a fast-growing area within WSU, known globally for our expertise in the most critical areas of aerospace research and development. We are seeking self-motivated, team-oriented teardown mechanics. Read more NIAR Engineering Program Manager 498894 Wichita Aviation Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration Wichita State University is looking for an experienced Program Manager to join our NIAR Team. The ideal candidate will have experience coordinating across functions and a good understanding of engineering design, analysis, and aircraft integration. This role will support both commercial and military programs. Read more NIAR Project Operations Manager 498536 Wichita Aviation Staff Office Ind & Defense Administration NIAR is seeking a detail‑driven and highly organized Project Operations Manager to support the successful planning, execution, and financial oversight of laboratory projects and grant‑funded initiatives. This role serves as a central operational partner—working closely with project teams, leadership, finance, and contracts—to ensure projects stay on track, align with approved scopes, meet sponsor expectations, and maintain compliance with internal and external requirements. The ideal candidate brings strong project management experience, a commitment to operational excellence, and the ability to navigate complex workflows to support NIAR’s mission and research programs. Read more Assistant/Associate Athletics Director of Shocker Media 499263 Wichita Athletics Staff Administrative and Support The Assistant/Associate Athletics Director of Shocker Media provides leadership for Wichita State Athletics' integrated communications unit. Shocker Media serves as the central hub for how Wichita State Athletics tells its story – connecting student-athletes, coaches, programs, and the Shocker brand with fans, donors, media, recruits, alumni, campus partners, and the greater community through strategic communications, digital content, social media, and live event broadcasts. Read more Admissions Evaluator 499207 Wichita Management/Administration Office/Administrative Support Staff Strategic Enrollment Mgmt The devil’s in the details. Your detailed eye is needed for reviewing multiple application materials and applying professional judgement on enrollment eligibility which in turn means you’re impacting students. If you are organized, like data entry & being a detective to solve problems or a combo of both with data cleanup then we encourage you to consider this position! Being able to handle fluctuating workloads as well as competing priorities with this team’s dynamics is the key to success here. Everyone has a part in recruiting & this position gets to show it all with the data they handle daily. Read more NetApp - Performance Engineer Student Assistant 495835 Wichita Student Natl Inst for Rsrch&Digtal Transfrm Ennovar is looking for a student assistant to work at NetApp. Read more Writing Specialist, TRIO SSS STEM 499165 Wichita Student Strategic Engagement & Planning The writing specialist provides high‑quality academic support to undergraduate participants in the federally funded TRIO Student Support Services – STEM Program. Tutors assist students in strengthening their understanding of course content, developing effective learning strategies, and building confidence in their academic abilities. Read more Student Assistant TRIO SSS 499146 Wichita Student Strategic Engagement & Planning Are you looking for a job where you can make a difference on campus while building your professional skills? TRIO Student Support Services is looking for a friendly and motivated Student Assistant to join our team! Read more NIAR CAMO Maintenance Support Technician 498925 Wichita Temporary NIAR Institute The Maintenance Support Technician ensures technicians have the tools, materials, and logistical support needed to perform efficiently. This position focuses on organization, transport, and readiness—helping keep the hangar running smoothly and safely. Read more NIAR CAMO Coordinator 498923 Wichita Temporary NIAR Institute In a hangar adjacent to McConnell AFB that once housed Boeing Air Force One modification facilities, the CAMO team at NIAR provides production design, initial and Supplemental Type Certification, instrumentation installation, modifications and field support/repair. We are looking for a Coordinator to join our fast-growing team! Read more Displaying 91 - 120 of 197 in total ‹ 1 2 3 4 5 6 7 › 1845 Fairmount St. Wichita , Kansas 67260 USA (316) 978-3456 Request Info Visit Apply Contact Us Virtual Tour Campus Map and Directions Facebook X | Twitter Instagram YouTube Linkedin People at Wichita State will make introductions, look for (applied learning) opportunities, and give advice that will put you miles ahead of others. Jon Peterson , senior in business administration and real estate finance Alumni & Friends Give to WSU A-Z Index Freedom of Expression Policies and Procedures Privacy Policy Notice of Nondiscrimination Title IX Campus Safety Accessibility Public Information Website Support KBOR Freedom of Expression Statement HLC Accreditation © 2024 Wichita State University Wichita State University (\"WSU\") does not discriminate on the basis of sex in its education programs, activities, admissions and employment. Candidate Details We use \"cookies\" on this site. A cookie is a piece of data stored on a site visitor's hard drive to help us improve your access to our site and identify repeat visitors to our site. For instance, when we use a cookie to identify you, you would not have to log in a password more than once, thereby saving time while on our site. Cookies can also enable us to track and target the interests of our users to enhance the experience on our site. Usage of a cookie is in no way linked to any personally identifiable information on our site. Some of our business partners may use cookies on our site (for example, Google Analytics). However, we have no access to or control over these cookies. I do not accept I accept"
